// Pull request: #6122 update: Regsvr32 detection rules tuning and expansion
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6122
// Pull request author: swachchhanda000
// Change: update to existing rule
// Title: Regsvr32 DLL Execution With Uncommon Extension
// Sigma ID: 50919691-7302-437f-8e10-1fe088afa145
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2019-07-17 | Modified: 2026-10-18
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, persistence, stealth, T1574, execution
// Description: Detects a "regsvr32" execution where the DLL doesn't contain a common file extension. Threat
//   actors often rename their malicious DLLs to often benign file extensions to avoid detection.
// False positives:
//   - Other legitimate extensions currently not in the list either from third party or specific Windows components.
// References:
//   - https://app.any.run/tasks/34221348-072d-4b70-93f3-aa71f6ebecad/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/fba4b94a2237d0ec8fe1cd5dc9c4c29dc6d3e4c4/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_regsvr32_uncommon_extension.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\regsvr32.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "REGSVR32.EXE") and (not(((ProcessCommandLine contains ".ax" or ProcessCommandLine contains ".cpl" or ProcessCommandLine contains ".dll" or ProcessCommandLine contains ".ocx") or isnull(ProcessCommandLine) or ProcessCommandLine =~ "" or (ProcessCommandLine in~ ("\"C:\\WINDOWS\\system32\\regsvr32.exe\"", "\"C:\\WINDOWS\\SysWOW64\\regsvr32.exe\""))))) and (not((ProcessCommandLine contains ".ppl" or ProcessCommandLine contains ".bav")))
